कक्षीवत् m. [कक्ष्या-मत् Mbh. on P. VI. 1. 37] N. of a renowned
 Ṛṣi, sometimes called Pajriya; author of several hymns of the Ṛgveda;
 कक्षीवन्तं य औशिजः Rv. 1. 18. 1.

काकः + -उलूकिका, -उलूकीयम् the natural enmity of the owl and the crow;
 Mbh. on IV. 2. 104; Vārt 2. (काकोलूकीयम् is the name of the third
 Tantra in the Pañcatantra).

